I don't see it as a problem, but demon-mapping is already a pretty
common way of finding your path through Gehennom.

Asmodeus in particular is not a threat at all, usually the course of
action is wake him, level teleport to the bottom of Gehennom, then beat
on him until he's wounded (be careful not to kill him), use ESP to
locate him at the upstairs, teleport over, drag him up to the next
level with you, repeat.

If you lack the magic mapping spell and don't have a spare marker, it's
a pretty quick way to skip exploring all the levels down there.  You
still have to locate Vlad's seperately, but that's a smaller task than
finding all of the stairs.

Like I said, I don't think it's necessarily a problem, but I don't like
that a big purple & is such a pushover that people regularly say things
like "use a stethoscope to make sure you don't kill him!"



